{
  "comment": "SDE theme palettes: the single source of the colors and shapes of every SDE theme family. tools/build-themes.py uses it for the GTK overlays, libadwaita colors and Openbox themes, and writes generated/theme_palettes.h for sde::Theme (src/common/theme.cpp). Colors are #RRGGBB; shadow_alpha, mica and translucency are 0-1. Since 0.1.0~alpha51 the palettes are calm, low-chroma neutrals (Graphite neutral, Fluent cool slate, Glass warm stone) with muted accents, and every family has soft corners (radius_small for buttons and fields, radius for windows, menus and cards, radius_large for big surfaces). Caption buttons are on the right (minimize, maximize, close) in the style of Mint-Y: thin small glyphs, a soft gray disc behind the close cross (and behind the other glyphs while hovered), a muted red close only while hovered; caption sets the hit area in percent of the title height, the spacing in pixels and that red.",
